  "config": {
    "_comment": "Colours: yellow = warning, red = near critical. Tyre temperature is the air inside the tyre: blue under tyreCold, yellow within 15 C of tyreHot, red from tyreHot. Tyre pressure against the car's target: yellow over 1 psi off, red over 3 psi (UNEVEN against the other side of the axle when the car sends no target). Boost against target (only while the target is over 0.2 bar): yellow 0.15 bar (2.2 psi) off, red 0.3 bar (4.4 psi). Low pressure fuel (engine running): yellow under 4 bar, red under 3. Fuel rail: yellow under 25 bar, red under 15. Gearbox oil: yellow from 110 C, red from 125. Outside: yellow at 3 C and below (ice). Range: yellow under 80 km, red under 40. Intercooler: air after it yellow from 50 C, red from 60 C; heat soak (after minus outside) yellow from 20 C (36 F), red from 30 C (54 F).",
    "dme": {
      "comment": "Read from the engine unit (DME, ecu 18) with UDS 0x22 over the kit's read-only link, only while the page shows; candidates are tried in order, the first plausible one wins (value = raw * factor + offset). The identifiers M Vitals reads (cauliflowermossgrape, MIT). boostTarget / boostActual: boost setpoint and actual, absolute kPa (the outside air pressure, baro, is subtracted). hpfp: fuel rail (high pressure) bar. lpfp: low pressure fuel bar. loadTarget / loadActual: requested and actual relative air charge %. egs: gearbox oil temperature from the gearbox unit (ecu 24), asked only while the car's basic data set has none. chargeBefore / intake: the charge air before the throttle (ahead of the B58's water-to-air intercooler) and in the plenum after it: the intercooler's drop and heat soak (after minus outside). The B58 has no temperature sensor in the intercooler's water circuit.",
      "ecu": 18,
      "baro": [
        {
          "did": "4201",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 0.00390625,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "IPUMG, ambient pressure, u16 x 0.0390625 hPa -> kPa. DME8FF_R (MG1 DME: B58 / B48 / B38, G series), the identifiers cauliflowermossgrape's Live Data reads (MIT)"
        },
        {
          "did": "F433",
          "bytes": 1,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 1,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "OBD PID 0x33 barometric pressure, kPa (101.3 when not available)"
        },
        {
          "obd": "33",
          "bytes": 1,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 1,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "OBD service 01 PID 0x33 (same as F433)"
        }
      ],
